def trow(r,use):
    h,p=cheapest(r);return f"<tr><td><b>{r}&nbsp;GB</b></td><td>{use}</td><td><b>${p['renewal_price_mo']:.2f}</b>/mo<br><span class=small>{h['name']} {p['name']}</span></td></tr>"
q=[("How much RAM does n8n need?","n8n's own docs give 320 MB to 2 GB as an example range, and an idle n8n Cloud instance uses about 100 MB. On a VPS that also runs the OS and Docker, plan on 2 GB minimum for light personal use and 4 GB if you add Postgres, AI agent workflows or the Code node on large data."),
 ("Is 1 GB of RAM enough for n8n?","It can start, but there is very little headroom once the OS and Docker are running; a single large execution can crash it. 2 GB is a safer floor."),
 ("What uses the most memory in n8n?","Per n8n's docs: large JSON or binary data, the Code node (it copies data before and after running), manual executions (n8n keeps a copy for the editor), and several workflows running at the same time.")]
C.append(("compare/how-much-ram-does-n8n-need.html","How Much RAM Does n8n Need? (Self-Hosting Guide) | StackCost","How much memory self-hosted n8n really needs, what eats RAM, how to spot out-of-memory errors, and the cheapest VPS at 2, 4 and 8 GB by renewal price.",f'''<h1>How much RAM does n8n need?</h1><div class="prose"><p><b>Short answer: 2 GB to start, 4 GB to be comfortable.</b> {q[0][1]}</p></div>
<h2>RAM by use case — cheapest plan that fits</h2><div style="overflow-x:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>RAM</th><th>Good for</th><th>Cheapest (renewal)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(trow(r,u) for r,u in tiers)}</tbody></table></div>
<p>Worth knowing: {lo[0]['name']} {lo[1]['name']} ({lo[1]['vcpu']} vCPU / {lo[1]['ram_gb']} GB) renews at ${lo[1]['renewal_price_mo']:.2f}/mo{' (its regular list price after the 24-month intro)' if lo[0]['id']=='contabo' else ''} — the cheapest verified plan of <i>any</i> size, so going bigger doesn't always cost more.</p><p class="small">Verified USD VPS plans ranked by renewal price, checked {U}. Hetzner (EUR excl. VAT): {hzs(2)}; {hzs(4)}. Rule of thumb, not a benchmark.</p>
<div class="prose"><h2>What actually eats memory</h2><ul><li><b>Data size per execution</b> — big JSON responses and binary files (PDFs, images) sit in memory while a workflow runs.</li><li><b>The Code node</b> makes a copy of the data before and after it runs.</li><li><b>Manual test runs</b> — n8n keeps an extra copy for the editor.</li><li><b>Concurrency</b> — several workflows at once add up.</li><li><b>Extras on the same box</b> — Postgres, Redis (queue mode) and a reverse proxy each need their own RAM.</li></ul>
<h2>Signs you’ve run out</h2><p>“Execution stopped at this node (n8n may have run out of memory)”, “Connection Lost”, 503 errors, or <code>JavaScript heap out of memory</code> in the logs. The Docker image restarts n8n on its own; an npm install may need a manual restart.</p>
<h2>Try these before paying for more RAM</h2><ul><li>Process data in batches (Loop Over Items + a sub-workflow that returns only a small result).</li><li>Avoid the Code node for heavy lifting where a built-in node works.</li><li>Don’t test huge datasets with manual runs.</li><li>Raise Node’s heap with <code>NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=…</code> and add a swap file as a buffer.</li></ul>
<p>Next: <a href="can-n8n-run-on-2gb-ram.html">Can n8n run on 2 GB?</a> · <a href="cheapest-vps-for-n8n.html">Cheapest VPS for n8n</a> · <a href="../calculator.html">Calculator</a> (it picks a RAM size from your execution count).</p>
<p class="small">Sources: n8n docs — <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/deploy/host-n8n/configure-n8n/scaling/fix-memory-issues" rel="nofollow">Fix memory issues</a>, <a href="https://docs.n8n.io/deploy/host-n8n/deploy-as-an-oem-integration/prerequisites" rel="nofollow">sizing prerequisites</a>.</p></div>''',faq(q)))
